{
 "about": "Spandrel sprig of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left spandrel, drawn by hand as smooth curves while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Bands are raised ribbons along Catmull-Rom centre lines; beads are domes (flower petals, berries). The hatched field around them is the panel ground.  Position and size follow the Palace Museum album: the drawing sits 3 album px lower than the panel corner mapping gives, as the two impressions differ by that much here. Below the loop (stem, hook, side branch, small leaf and tail) the control points were re-read on album_2 at 1 px, as the earlier ones ran too far left and down there. The right spandrel is the mirror image of this one about the gate axis.",
